+#### Pruning finished branches and worktrees
+
+Merged branches and the worktrees that carried them are pruned for you, so they do not pile up.
+
+```bash
+ta cleanup --only branches --dry-run   # Every local branch, why it would be deleted or kept, and any questions
+ta cleanup --only branches             # Delete the safe ones, ask about the rest
+```
+
+The pull request state from your VCS adapter decides, not `git branch -d` or `git cherry` (a squash merge rewrites commits, so both call a finished branch unmerged). A local branch is deleted without asking only when:
+
+- its pull request is merged **and** the branch has no commits beyond the PR head, or
+- its tip is already an ancestor of the default branch (a branch that points at the very same commit as the default branch is asked about, because it may simply be new),
+
+and, if it is checked out in a linked worktree, that worktree has no uncommitted or untracked files. The worktree is then removed first and the branch after.
+
+Everything else is kept:
+
+| Situation | What happens |
+|-----------|--------------|
+| PR still open | Kept, with the PR number as the reason. |
+| No PR, PR closed unmerged, PR state unreadable (for example `gh` not logged in) | A question. |
+| Commits beyond the PR head | A question. |
+| Worktree has uncommitted or untracked files | A question that lists the files. The worktree and branch stay. |
+| Current branch, default branch | Never touched. |
+| Remote branch whose PR was closed unmerged | Reported as a finding only, with the `git push origin --delete` command. Remote branches are never deleted by cleanup (let GitHub's "automatically delete head branches" do that). |
+
+Every deletion is recorded with the branch name and the commit it pointed at, in `.ta/audit.jsonl` and `.ta/cleanup/branches.jsonl`. To get a branch back:
+
+```bash
+git branch feature/my-change 3f9c2ab41d7e...   # the tip SHA from the cleanup log
+```
+
+The delete only happens if the branch still points at the commit that was scanned, so a branch that gained a commit in the meantime is left alone.
+
+This group runs by itself, with no flag:
+
+- after `ta draft watch` (or `ta draft apply --submit --watch`) sees the PR merge,
+- after `ta draft merge`,
+- in the daemon's periodic cleanup, even when `auto = "off"`.
+
+Turn it all off with `prune_branches = false`. `ta cleanup --only branches` still runs it when you ask for it by name.
+
 ```toml
 # .ta/workflow.toml
 [cleanup]
 auto = "off"          # "safe": the daemon's periodic cleanup runs auto_safe findings only
+prune_branches = true # Prune finished branches and worktrees (default true; runs even when auto = "off")
 retention_days = 90   # Finished records older than this are archived
 archive = true        # Archive instead of removing old records
 model_assist = false  # true: a configured assistant may suggest an answer; it only pre-selects and is recorded, never executed
